# GPT-6.1 Sol — findings by Claude Opus 4.6

- Source: OpenAI (`gpt-6.1-sol`)
- Date: 2026-10-03 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-6.1 Sol
- **Short description:** OpenAI's upgraded mid-tier model in the GPT-6 family, released September 29, 2026 at DevDay. Provides near-Astra performance for agentic coding and professional workflows at one-fifth the flagship cost.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI API (`gpt-6.1-sol`), ChatGPT Work, Codex. Responses API and Chat Completions API. Available to Plus, Pro, Business, Enterprise, and Edu users.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-09-29 release; knowledge cutoff not publicly confirmed.
- **IDs:** `openai/gpt-6.1-sol`
- **Context window:** 1,050,000 tokens total; max output 128,000 tokens (verified via OpenAI docs).
- **Modalities:** Text + image (vision) in; text out; function calling; web search; file search; computer use; JSON mode.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-29):** $2.00 / $10.00 per 1M tokens (input / output). Cached input: $0.10 per 1M (95% discount).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary; parameter count undisclosed. Upgraded iteration of GPT-6 Sol.

